# =====================================================================
#  The Hour Between  -  Nocturne for Solo Cello and Strings
#  by Johann Sebastian Grok, for Simon.   B minor (-> B major), c. 6'50"
#  SGN score (format v1.1, see FORMAT.md at the root of this
#  repository) + extensions v1.2 as in KUMI ({ks:...}, CB floor c1).
#  Alternative title:  "Until the D-sharp"
# =====================================================================
# Everything in docs/sgn-v1.1-spec.txt holds
# (concert pitch, c4 = middle C, sticky durations, R / R*n, chords lowest
# first, ~ ties, x=32 measured, doubling lines =src -8 @bA-B {ks:..},
# HANDOFF blocks).  This file has NO notes.
#
# FILES (play in this order; bars are numbered continuously, all 4/4)
#   10-dusk.sgn            b1-14     1 Dusk           T=56 (52) -> 64        0:00.0
#   20-song.sgn            b15-42    2 Song           T=64 (60), rit. to 54  0:59.3
#   30-restless-hour.sgn   b43-65    3 Restless Hour  T=72-76-66, cadenza 60-44-50, 56  2:46.6
#   40-moonlight.sgn       b66-90    4 Moonlight      T=64 (60), rit. to 56  4:11.9
#   50-dawn.sgn            b91-104   5 Dawn           T=58 -> 54-52-50 -> 40 5:46.9
#   end of b104                                                             6:49.5
#   (times computed from T= and M= and cross-checked against
#    sgn2flp's tempo map)
#   Rubato is written as small tempo steps (@@ bN T=..) at phrase ends.
#   Every block's first bar repeats its tempo as  @@ bN T=..  so that
#   sgn2flp never drops a block-start tempo.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# E1. PART CODES (score order).
#   vcs   SOLO CELLO (Hollywood Solo Cello, monophonic)
#   vn1 vn2 va vc cb   Hollywood Strings sections.  A dyad with {div}
#         = divisi (use the DIV A patch for vn1 / va / vc if wanted;
#         articulation names are identical).  cb floor c1.
#
# E2. KEYSWITCH TOKEN {ks:<exact articulation name from the KS JSON>} is
#   sticky along its line; every keyswitched written line sets one before
#   its first note in every block; doubling lines carry exactly one.
#
# E3. ARTICULATIONS THAT DO NOT EXIST in these patches (KS JSON) and how
#   the score replaces them:
#     pizzicato  -> basses' "heartbeat" = Stac On Bow RRx9, soft, short
#     tremolo    -> measured 32nds (x=32) on Staccatissimo / Stac On Bow
#     con sord.  -> none; the hush is pp/ppp and thin spacing
#     harmonics  -> none; the final B5 is Sus NV NV VB Solo (senza vib.)
#
# E4. CONTRABASS FLOOR = c1 (sgn2flp: set CB_FLOOR = 24).
#   (This score's basses never go below e1 anyway.)
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# MATERIAL
#   THE SONG (vcs b15, vn1 8va b67, vcs in B major b91):
#     | f#4. b4 d5 - | c#5 d5 e5 d5 c#5 b4 | g5. f#5 e5 - | d5 c#5 b4 a#4 - |
#     a rising B-minor triad, a turn, the minor-sixth sigh B->G, the fall
#     to A#.  Its head F#-B-D is also the cello's first words (Dusk b2)
#     and its last shadow (Restless Hour b55, in G minor; b63, low).
#   LAMENT BASS  B - A - G - F#  under every statement of the Song.
#   NOCTURNE FIGURE  celli section, eighths, 4-note open voicings
#     (bass, 5th/3rd, octave, 3rd) in shapes 0123-2121 / 0123-2321;
#     basses' heartbeat on beats 1 and 3.
#   THE D-SHARP  the Song's third, turned major (b87 vn1, b91 vcs):
#     the whole piece waits for it.
# =====================================================================
